{"text": "\u201d, 4. PLEASE NOTE FINAL PARAGRAPH ON PAGE 1 HAS BEEN REVISED, \u201c\u2014\u2014~\n\nAugust 2, 1985\n\nTo: Mr. J, T, Winebrenner\nRE: STERLING BRAND PERSPECTIVE\nThe following report is preliminary information on the\nSTERLING Repositioning and is based solely on in-market\nobservations, The MDD tracking reports on STERLING will be\navailable on August 30, September 27, and November 1, 1985.\nOverall\n\n1. %In-market observations of STERLING 85 showed very\nminimal movement at the eight-week time period,\n\n1F displays were particularly indicative of minimal\nmovement. Even with a price deal, consumers appear to -\nhave little interest and/or awareness of the Brand\nstyle.\n\n3. Little evidence of covpon redemption was seen. Any\nredemption that was made appeared to be on the Box\nstyles only.\n\n4, Generally, even with the normal schedule of OOH and\nthe POS associated with STERLING's secondary position,\nthere was not much presence or impact perceived for\nthe Brand in any of the markets. This lack of\npresence was also perceived at retail as slow movement\nappeared to result in low retailer awareness.\n\nWhile Little movement has been seen at retail during the\neight-week time period, MDD tracking reports, beginning the\nend of August, will provide a more quantifiable assessment\nof the Brand.\n\nThe STERLING BIGIF program was set at 16M cases, as opposed\nto the normal 25M cases, in anticipation of lower potential\nvolume assumptions for this line extension and reposition-\ning. There does remain, at the present time, about 3,400\navailable cases of B1G1F product. Of these 3,400 cases,\n2,600 cases were produced for a B1G1F, without coupons, to\nbe worked on STERLING 85 in the PMSA during 3rd Quarter, At\nthe present time, a little over 800 cases have been ordered\nfor the PMSA, and the Brand Group will continue to monitor\nusage until all orders are complete. There are also\napproximately 800 available cases remaining which contain\ncoupons dve to expire August 31, Rather than paying labor\ncosts to remove these coupons, the Brand recommends\ndestroying these cases and just using the remaining 2,600\ncases without covpons for any additional orders.\n\nteze 6199s", "words": [{"text": "\u201d,", "x0": 48, "y0": 25, "x1": 63, "y1": 37, "conf": 0.0}, {"text": "4.", "x0": 74, "y0": 32, "x1": 118, "y1": 40, "conf": 35.0}, {"text": "PLEASE", "x0": 126, "y0": 27, "x1": 178, "y1": 38, "conf": 89.0}, {"text": "NOTE", "x0": 188, "y0": 27, "x1": 222, "y1": 37, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "FINAL", "x0": 232, "y0": 26, "x1": 274, "y1": 36, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "PARAGRAPH", "x0": 284, "y0": 26, "x1": 361, "y1": 35, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "ON", "x0": 371, "y0": 25, "x1": 388, "y1": 35, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "PAGE", "x0": 398, "y0": 25, "x1": 431, "y1": 35, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "1", "x0": 442, "y0": 24, "x1": 449, "y1": 34, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "HAS", "x0": 460, "y0": 25, "x1": 484, "y1": 34, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "BEEN", "x0": 494, "y0": 25, "x1": 528, "y1": 34, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "REVISED,", "x0": 538, "y0": 25, "x1": 604, "y1": 35, "conf": 72.0}, {"text": "\u201c\u2014\u2014~", "x0": 626, "y0": 25, "x1": 670, "y1": 28, "conf": 35.0}, {"text": "August", "x0": 463, "y0": 75, "x1": 514, "y1": 87, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "2,", "x0": 525, "y0": 75, "x1": 539, "y1": 86, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "1985", "x0": 551, "y0": 75, "x1": 583, "y1": 85, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "To:", "x0": 114, "y0": 141, "x1": 138, "y1": 151, "conf": 61.0}, {"text": "Mr.", "x0": 158, "y0": 141, "x1": 182, "y1": 151, "conf": 85.0}, {"text": "J,", "x0": 194, "y0": 140, "x1": 208, "y1": 151, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "T,", "x0": 219, "y0": 140, "x1": 234, "y1": 150, "conf": 42.0}, {"text": "Winebrenner", "x0": 245, "y0": 139, "x1": 341, "y1": 150, "conf": 90.0}, {"text": "RE:", "x0": 115, "y0": 171, "x1": 138, "y1": 181, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "STERLING", "x0": 159, "y0": 170, "x1": 227, "y1": 181, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "BRAND", "x0": 237, 